---
description: When ticket work is finished, report what is not synced and ask with a selection form
alwaysApply: true
---

When the work for a ticket is finished, check the closeout before the reply ends. This includes `/ticket NB-xx` after the acceptance work, and any later pass that changes that ticket.

Check each item. Say in the reply which ones are still open. Name local, Linear, or both. Name commit, push, and merge only when that step has not happened.

- **Local.** The ticket file still has an open acceptance box for work that was verified, or `status` is not `Done` after that work.
- **Linear.** The local description or status was not sent after the last edit. Description uses `node scripts/linear-sync.mjs push-one <id>`. Status uses `node scripts/linear-sync.mjs set-status <id> Done --push`.
- **Commit.** The ticket branch has uncommitted work for this ticket.
- **Push.** The ticket branch is ahead of its remote, or has no upstream.
- **Merge.** A Phase 2 ticket (`parent: NB-E6`) is not on `phase-2`. Merge that branch into `phase-2` only. Any other ticket is not on `main`.

If every item is done, say that in one sentence and do not ask.

If any item is open, use AskQuestion before doing those steps. `allow_multiple` is true. Offer only the open steps, in this order, plus the two choices below. Put "Do the remaining steps" first.

- Do the remaining steps
- Update the local ticket
- Update Linear
- Commit
- Push
- Merge into phase-2
- Merge into main
- Leave it as it is

"Merge into phase-2" is only for a Phase 2 ticket. "Merge into main" is only for a ticket whose parent is not `NB-E6`. Do not offer a merge that the phase-2 rule forbids.

Wait for the selection. Then do the chosen steps in the order above. "Do the remaining steps" means every open step. "Leave it as it is" means change nothing else.
